              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was my first time cooking a full meal for my family, and it was a huge sucess. I was able to do something my mother and super-cheif aunt could'nt do, make a spaghetti sauce from scrach. All the high praises mean alot to a 20 year college guy. Thank you."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TxCin2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is delicious sauce. It's rich, thick, slightly sweet, not too tomatoey, and it's a kid friendly sauce as there are no chunks of tomatoes, peppers, or mushrooms to pick out. All of which I'd still pick out as an adult. It didn't say how long to cook this once you've gotten it hot throughout, but I let this simmer a while since I had the time because spaghetti sauce is one of those dishes that is better the longer it cooks. I used half a large sweet onion, and it was plenty of onion for my tastes. I'd estimate it was probably a good 3/4 cups' worth. As there is quite a bit of sugar, I added a pinch of crushed red pepper to tame down the sweet factor a smidge. This was a really good sauce and I would definitely make this one again. I ended up letting it simmer for 3 hours because that's how much time I had to let it do so. I added a little water as needed to keep it at the desired consistency. Thanks for posting this, we had a really nice meal.",
            "datePublished": "2026-06-11T01:31:38.049Z"
          },
          {
